{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790259167,"nonce":"Syne6UhAjrXVYamE/MIRF+g33JA=","title":"Python: a dynamic slice of an array boxes the whole array first","message":"zb_any_getslice's custom-kind arm was zb_list_box_any(slice_any(iter(x))),\nand the frontend's shaped items hook for a boxed array is\nzb_list_to_any_u8(raw): every 16-byte slice of pyaes's 92000-byte array\nboxed all 92000 elements into a List\u003cAny\u003e (736 KB written, realloc-copied\nand collected) before taking 16. That was most of crypto_pyaes's time on\nthe NUC (3.5 to 4.9 s per iteration at dea6d08b against PyPy's 25 to 40 ms).\n\narray('B', \u003cdynamic\u003e) also went through the items of whatever it was\nhanded, so bytes arriving as Object were boxed byte by byte, unlike the\ntyped array('B', bytes) path.\n\nFix: zb_any_getslice slices int, float and str lists at their kind, and\nasks a new zb_hook_shaped_getslice hook for shaped lists and arrays; the\nfrontend's hook slices the storage and boxes it under the source's tag,\nso the result is an array of the same typecode. array(code, \u003cdynamic\u003e)\ncopies bytes the way the typed path does and converts anything else\nthrough its items.","files":null}]}